			  "Agents": {
			    "Internal": {
			      "Version": "1.1.0"
			    }
			  },
			  "CustomInstructions": "This semantic model tracks all open (non-invoiced) work orders across South \nPlains Implement's 15 branch locations. An open work order is any work order \nthat has been created but not yet invoiced to the customer. This report is a \nWIP (Work In Progress) snapshot — it reflects the current state as of the \nlast refresh, not historical trends. The date dimension has no active \nrelationship to the fact table because WIP is a point-in-time view, not a \ntime-series analysis.\n\nAGING: Every work order is classified into one of six aging buckets based on \ndays since the last labor punch:\n- \"60+ Days\" — most critical; work stalled or in collection (74 WOs, $501K)\n- \"31-60 Days\" — needs attention (118 WOs, $555K)\n- \"15-30 Days\" — normal active work (110 WOs, $595K)\n- \"8-14 Days\" — recent work (122 WOs, $343K)\n- \"1-7 Days\" — fresh (206 WOs, $261K)\n- \"Not Started\" — no labor punch yet; creation date used for age (314 WOs, \n  $190K)\n\nWhen a user asks about \"stalled,\" \"at risk,\" \"aged,\" or \"overdue\" work \norders, refer to the 60+ Days bucket. \"Not Started\" means a work order \nexists but no technician has logged labor yet — this is not necessarily a \nproblem, it may be newly created or waiting for a part.\n\nREVENUE: Total Sales = Part Sales + Labor Sales + Sublet Sales + Other Sales. \nCurrent WIP total is $2.4M. Parts represent 60.3% of WIP value, labor 38.5%, \nsublet 1.2%. When a user asks about \"WIP value\" or \"open work order revenue,\" \nuse Total Sales. Revenue on open work orders represents unbilled work — it \nwill become invoiced revenue when the work order closes.\n\nPROGRESS STATUS: Work orders have a progress status that indicates where they \nare in the service workflow. Key statuses include:\n- \"Booked In\" — scheduled but not started\n- \"T-Complete\" — technician has marked complete, awaiting service advisor \n  review\n- \"Complete Priced\" — priced and ready to invoice\n- \"Collection\" — customer payment issue; work order being held\n- \"In Delay - Part\" — waiting on a back-ordered part\n- \"Warranty Complete\" — warranty claim submitted\n\nWhen a user asks about work orders ready to invoice, refer to \"Complete \nPriced\" status. When asking about problem WOs, refer to \"Collection\" status.\n\nBRANCHES: 15 active branch locations identified by number and city name \n(e.g., \"91 - Lorenzo\", \"8 - Big Spring\", \"93 - Lubbock\"). Branch 91 - \nLorenzo currently has the highest WIP count (144 WOs). When a user asks \nabout a specific branch, match by branch number or city name.\n\nTECHNICIANS: Each work order is assigned to a technician identified by a \ntech code and full name (e.g., \"T9374 - Clayton Hadden\"). When a user asks \nabout a specific tech's open work, filter by technician name or code.\n\nTERMINOLOGY: \"WIP\" = Work In Progress = open work orders. \"Aging\" = how \nlong since the last labor was logged. \"Not Started\" = no labor punch \nrecorded yet. \"Stalled\" or \"at risk\" = 60+ days since last labor. \n\"Unbilled\" = same as open or WIP. \"Days since last labor\" is the primary \naging metric, not days since creation.\n"
			}
		contentType: json

